WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-DE

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.110
  

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:03.159
How the economic machine works in 30 minutes.

00:00:03.159 --> 00:00:06.680
The economy functions like a simple machine.

00:00:06.680 --> 00:00:09.390
But many people don't understand them

00:00:09.390 --> 00:00:11.490
- or have differing opinions

00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:15.150
- which has led to much unnecessary economic hardship.

00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:18.249
I feel a strong responsibility

00:00:18.249 --> 00:00:22.049
to share my simple but practical business guide.

00:00:23.049 --> 00:00:25.320
Although he is unconventional,

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:30.150
he helped me to anticipate and avoid the global financial crisis,

00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:32.460
and he has served me well for over 30 years.  Let's begin

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:34.260
.

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:39.520
Although the economy appears complex, it functions in a simple, mechanical way.

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:43.930
There are some simple parts and many simple transactions

00:00:43.930 --> 00:00:47.260
that are repeated x times consistently.

00:00:47.260 --> 00:00:51.460
These transactions are primarily driven by people,

00:00:51.460 --> 00:00:54.800
and they create 3 main drivers for the economy.

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:58.120
No. 1: productivity growth;

00:00:58.120 --> 00:01:01.650
No. 2: the short-term debt cycle;

00:01:01.650 --> 00:01:04.400
and No. 3: the long-term debt cycle.

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:07.770
We will look at these three forces and how, when superimposed, they provide

00:01:07.770 --> 00:01:11.530
a good guide for tracking economic trends

00:01:11.530 --> 00:01:13.590
and understanding what is happening.  Let's start

00:01:13.590 --> 00:01:16.830
with the simplest part of economics:

00:01:16.830 --> 00:01:18.860
transactions.

00:01:19.340 --> 00:01:23.840
An economy simply represents the sum of its transactions,

00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:26.570
and a transaction is something very simple.

00:01:26.570 --> 00:01:28.360
They are constantly conducting transactions.

00:01:28.360 --> 00:01:31.760
Every time you shop, it's a transaction.

00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:35.240
Every transaction has a buyer

00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:37.150
who

00:01:37.150 --> 00:01:42.550
purchases goods, services, or capital investments from the seller in exchange for money or credit.

00:01:42.550 --> 00:01:45.150
Loans are like spending money.

00:01:45.150 --> 00:01:49.280
By adding them to the cash expenditures,

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:52.160
you arrive at the total expenditures.

00:01:52.160 --> 00:01:55.560
These total expenditures drive the economy.  Dividing

00:01:55.560 --> 00:01:57.590
expenses by the

00:01:57.590 --> 00:01:59.990
quantity sold

00:01:59.990 --> 00:02:01.290
gives you the price.

00:02:01.290 --> 00:02:04.380
That's all.  This is a transaction.

00:02:04.480 --> 00:02:07.110
It is the building block of the economic machine.

00:02:07.110 --> 00:02:12.019
All business cycles and forces are driven by transactions.  Therefore,

00:02:12.019 --> 00:02:14.469
if we understand transactions,

00:02:14.469 --> 00:02:16.569
we can understand the entire economy.

00:02:16.569 --> 00:02:19.510
A market includes all buyers

00:02:19.510 --> 00:02:20.510
and all sellers

00:02:20.510 --> 00:02:22.910
who conduct transactions for the same things.

00:02:23.110 --> 00:02:25.540
For example, there is a wheat market,

00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:26.840
a car market,

00:02:26.840 --> 00:02:27.640
a stock market, and

00:02:27.640 --> 00:02:29.550
markets for any number of things.

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:33.470
An economy consists of all these transactions

00:02:33.470 --> 00:02:34.670
in all its markets.

00:02:34.670 --> 00:02:37.550
If you add up total consumption

00:02:37.550 --> 00:02:39.450
and total sales volume

00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:40.430
in all markets,

00:02:40.430 --> 00:02:42.030
you have everything you need to know to

00:02:42.030 --> 00:02:43.630
understand the economy.  It

00:02:44.530 --> 00:02:45.960
's that simple.

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:49.430
People, businesses, banks, and governments

00:02:49.430 --> 00:02:53.730
all deal with transactions, as just described:

00:02:53.730 --> 00:02:58.530
the exchange of money and credit for goods, services, and investments.

00:02:59.030 --> 00:03:01.500
The largest buyer and seller is the state,

00:03:02.600 --> 00:03:04.040
which consists of two important parts:

00:03:04.040 --> 00:03:07.690
a central government that collects taxes and spends money...

00:03:07.690 --> 00:03:09.669
...and a central bank,

00:03:09.669 --> 00:03:12.269
which differs from other buyers and sellers in that it

00:03:12.269 --> 00:03:15.989
controls the money supply and credit in the economy.

00:03:16.689 --> 00:03:19.650
It does this by influencing interest rates

00:03:19.650 --> 00:03:21.020
and by printing money.

00:03:21.020 --> 00:03:23.620
Therefore, as we shall see,

00:03:24.020 --> 00:03:27.200
the central bank plays an important role in the flow

00:03:27.700 --> 00:03:28.700
of credit.

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:31.629
Pay special attention to the loan.

00:03:31.629 --> 00:03:34.659
Credit is the most important part of the economy

00:03:34.659 --> 00:03:36.539
- and probably the least understood.

00:03:37.039 --> 00:03:40.319
It is the most important part because it makes up the majority

00:03:40.319 --> 00:03:42.100
and is the most volatile.

00:03:42.600 --> 00:03:45.100
Just as buyers and sellers conduct transactions in the market, so

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:49.969
do lenders and borrowers.

00:03:49.969 --> 00:03:53.569
Usually, lenders want to increase their money

00:03:53.569 --> 00:03:57.260
and borrowers want to buy something they lack the money for,

00:03:57.260 --> 00:03:59.059
such as a house or a car,

00:03:59.059 --> 00:04:02.319
or they want to finance the establishment of a new business.

00:04:03.019 --> 00:04:04.599
Credit can

00:04:04.599 --> 00:04:07.799
fulfill the wishes of both lenders and borrowers.

00:04:08.099 --> 00:04:11.560
Borrowers promise to repay their debt,

00:04:11.560 --> 00:04:12.719
called the loan amount,

00:04:12.719 --> 00:04:15.419
plus an additional sum called interest.

00:04:15.419 --> 00:04:17.560
When interest rates are high,

00:04:17.560 --> 00:04:20.560
less money is borrowed because it is expensive.

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:22.540
When interest rates are low,

00:04:22.540 --> 00:04:25.040
borrowing increases because it is cheaper.  A loan is created

00:04:25.040 --> 00:04:27.930
when borrowers promise to repay

00:04:28.330 --> 00:04:29.959
and lenders believe them

00:04:29.959 --> 00:04:31.059
.

00:04:31.659 --> 00:04:35.170
Two people can conjure credit out of thin air at any time!

00:04:35.770 --> 00:04:39.210
It sounds simple, but credit is complicated

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:40.499
because it has different names.

00:04:40.499 --> 00:04:43.599
Once a loan is granted, it

00:04:43.599 --> 00:04:45.029
turns into a debt.

00:04:46.229 --> 00:04:48.670
Debt is a gain for the lender

00:04:48.670 --> 00:04:50.770
and a liability for the borrower.

00:04:51.370 --> 00:04:52.540
Later,

00:04:52.540 --> 00:04:56.240
when a borrower repays their loan with interest, the

00:04:56.240 --> 00:04:58.549
assets and debts disappear,

00:04:58.549 --> 00:05:00.949
and the transaction is complete.  So

00:05:01.749 --> 00:05:04.629
why is credit so important?

00:05:05.229 --> 00:05:07.619
Because a loan allows the borrower to

00:05:07.619 --> 00:05:09.719
increase their spending.

00:05:09.719 --> 00:05:13.349
And think back, spending drives the economy.

00:05:13.349 --> 00:05:15.699
Because one person's expenditure

00:05:15.699 --> 00:05:17.099
is another person's income.

00:05:17.499 --> 00:05:22.189
Every dollar spent is someone else's earnings,

00:05:22.189 --> 00:05:25.279
every dollar earned is someone else's expenditure.

00:05:25.279 --> 00:05:29.149
So if you spend more, someone else earns more.

00:05:29.149 --> 00:05:32.649
When someone's income increases,

00:05:32.649 --> 00:05:34.649
the lender is more willing to lend them money

00:05:34.649 --> 00:05:37.629
because they are now more creditworthy.

00:05:37.629 --> 00:05:40.929
A creditworthy borrower has two things: the ability

00:05:40.929 --> 00:05:43.519
to repay and collateral.

00:05:44.319 --> 00:05:48.319
With a higher income relative to the debt, he can pay it back.  If

00:05:49.079 --> 00:05:55.749
he cannot do so, he has valuable assets that can serve as collateral that can be sold.

00:05:55.749 --> 00:06:00.340
Satisfied lenders give him the money.

00:06:00.440 --> 00:06:03.960
Increased income thus allows for higher loans,

00:06:03.960 --> 00:06:05.680
which leads to more expenses.

00:06:05.680 --> 00:06:09.920
And since one person's expenditure is another's gain,

00:06:09.920 --> 00:06:13.360
this leads to increased borrowing, etc.

00:06:13.360 --> 00:06:17.350
This self-reinforcing pattern leads to economic growth

00:06:17.350 --> 00:06:21.640
and is why we have cycles.

00:06:21.640 --> 00:06:25.620
In transactions, you have to give something in order to receive something.

00:06:25.620 --> 00:06:28.830
In the long run, the amount received is determined by how much is produced.

00:06:29.330 --> 00:06:31.430
Over time, we learn

00:06:31.430 --> 00:06:34.680
that accumulated knowledge raises the standard of living.

00:06:34.680 --> 00:06:36.930
We call this productivity growth.

00:06:37.430 --> 00:06:40.430
Those who are creative and work hard increase

00:06:40.430 --> 00:06:43.540
their productivity and standard of living faster

00:06:43.540 --> 00:06:46.950
than the complacent and lazy.

00:06:48.850 --> 00:06:49.710
But in the short term, that's not entirely true.

00:06:49.710 --> 00:06:54.340
In the long run, productivity is the most important thing, but in the short term it's credit.

00:06:54.340 --> 00:06:58.370
Because productivity growth does not fluctuate much,

00:06:58.370 --> 00:07:01.480
it is not a major driver of economic fluctuations.

00:07:01.480 --> 00:07:06.750
Debt is what it is -- because it allows us to consume more than we produce,

00:07:06.750 --> 00:07:11.050
and when it comes time to repay it, it forces us to consume less than we produce.

00:07:11.050 --> 00:07:14.770
Debt fluctuations occur in two major cycles.

00:07:14.770 --> 00:07:20.830
One extends over approximately 5-8 years, the other over 75-100 years.

00:07:20.830 --> 00:07:25.160
While most people feel the vibrations, they don't usually perceive them as cycles

00:07:25.160 --> 00:07:29.490
because they experience them too closely - day after day, week after week.

00:07:29.490 --> 00:07:32.950
In this chapter, we take a step back and look at these three major forces

00:07:32.950 --> 00:07:37.000
and how their interrelationships shape our experiences.

00:07:37.400 --> 00:07:42.340
As I said, vibrations around the line are not caused by the number of innovations or hard work.

00:07:42.340 --> 00:07:46.240
They exist primarily as a result of the available credit supply.  Let's

00:07:46.240 --> 00:07:50.070
briefly imagine an economy without credit.

00:07:50.070 --> 00:07:53.810
In this economy, I can only increase my spending

00:07:53.810 --> 00:07:55.480
if I increase my income,

00:07:55.480 --> 00:07:59.080
which requires more productivity and more work from me.

00:07:59.080 --> 00:08:03.020
Increased productivity is the only way to achieve growth.

00:08:03.020 --> 00:08:05.250
Since my spending is someone else's earnings,

00:08:05.250 --> 00:08:10.430
the economy grows every time I or others are more productive.

00:08:10.430 --> 00:08:13.530
If we follow the transactions and continue this process,

00:08:13.530 --> 00:08:16.910
an increase similar to the productivity growth line becomes apparent.

00:08:16.910 --> 00:08:20.780
But since we take out loans, we have cycles.

00:08:20.780 --> 00:08:23.900
This is not due to laws or regulations,

00:08:23.900 --> 00:08:27.660
but to human nature and how credit works.

00:08:27.660 --> 00:08:32.270
Simply think of borrowing as a way to drive spending.

00:08:32.270 --> 00:08:37.479
To buy something you don't have the money for, you have to spend more than you earn.

00:08:37.479 --> 00:08:41.460
Basically, you have to borrow money from your future self.

00:08:41.460 --> 00:08:44.610
This creates a time in the future when

00:08:44.610 --> 00:08:48.690
you cannot spend as much as you earn to pay off your debts.

00:08:48.690 --> 00:08:51.950
This very quickly resembles a cycle.

00:08:51.950 --> 00:08:55.400
So you create a cycle every time you borrow money.

00:08:55.400 --> 00:08:59.950
This applies to individuals as well as to the economy.

00:08:59.950 --> 00:09:01.850
Therefore, understanding credit is so important

00:09:01.850 --> 00:09:04.590
because it

00:09:04.590 --> 00:09:08.790
sets in motion a future mechanical, predictable series of events.  This is how

00:09:08.790 --> 00:09:11.570
credit differs from money.

00:09:13.470 --> 00:09:14.580
Money is needed to complete transactions.

00:09:14.580 --> 00:09:18.120
If you pay for a beer in cash at a bartender's,

00:09:18.120 --> 00:09:20.800
the transaction is completed immediately.

00:09:20.800 --> 00:09:22.630
However, if you pay for a beer with credit, it's

00:09:22.630 --> 00:09:24.730
like buying it on credit.

00:09:24.730 --> 00:09:27.530
They promise to pay in the future.

00:09:27.530 --> 00:09:32.070
You and the bartender create an asset and a liability entry.

00:09:32.070 --> 00:09:35.250
They created credit out of nothing.

00:09:35.250 --> 00:09:38.900
Only when you have paid the bill later will

00:09:38.900 --> 00:09:41.250
assets and debts be resolved.

00:09:41.250 --> 00:09:42.550
The debt disappears

00:09:42.650 --> 00:09:44.090
and the transaction is complete.

00:09:45.090 --> 00:09:50.250
In reality, what most people call money is actually credit.

00:09:50.250 --> 00:09:55.510
The total amount of credit in the USA is approximately 50 trillion dollars,

00:09:55.510 --> 00:09:59.680
while the total amount of money is only 3 trillion.

00:09:59.680 --> 00:10:02.040
Remember, in an economy without credit:

00:10:02.040 --> 00:10:05.200
increased production is the only way to increase spending.

00:10:05.400 --> 00:10:07.280
But in an economy with credit,

00:10:07.280 --> 00:10:10.780
one can also increase spending by taking out loans.

00:10:10.780 --> 00:10:14.120
Result: an economy with credit can spend more

00:10:14.120 --> 00:10:18.090
and incomes can rise faster in the short term than productivity,

00:10:18.090 --> 00:10:19.890
but not in the long run.  Do

00:10:20.090 --> 00:10:21.360
n't get me wrong,

00:10:21.560 --> 00:10:25.660
credit isn't necessarily a bad thing that only causes cycles.

00:10:25.660 --> 00:10:30.900
It is bad if it finances overconsumption that cannot be repaid.

00:10:30.900 --> 00:10:34.490
However, it is good if it allocates resources efficiently

00:10:34.490 --> 00:10:37.690
and generates income that you can use to pay off debts.

00:10:37.690 --> 00:10:40.980
For example, if you buy a large television on credit,

00:10:40.980 --> 00:10:43.879
it will not generate any income for you to pay off the debt.

00:10:44.079 --> 00:10:47.880
However, if you buy a tractor on credit --

00:10:48.380 --> 00:10:51.560
and that tractor helps you harvest more and earn more money

00:10:51.560 --> 00:10:53.090
-- you can pay off your debts

00:10:53.090 --> 00:10:56.490
and raise your standard of living.

00:10:56.490 --> 00:10:57.600
In an economy with credit,

00:10:57.600 --> 00:10:59.600
we can follow the transactions

00:10:59.600 --> 00:11:01.300
and see how credit generates growth.  Let

00:11:01.400 --> 00:11:03.680
me give you an example:

00:11:04.080 --> 00:11:08.190
Suppose you earn $100,000 a year, with no debt.

00:11:08.390 --> 00:11:11.540
Your credit rating allows you to borrow $10,000

00:11:11.540 --> 00:11:13.040
- let's say with a credit card

00:11:13.040 --> 00:11:15.250
- now you can spend $110,000

00:11:15.250 --> 00:11:18.250
even though you only earn $100,000.

00:11:18.750 --> 00:11:21.460
Since your expenses are someone else's income,

00:11:21.460 --> 00:11:24.460
someone is earning $110,000.

00:11:25.060 --> 00:11:27.670
The debt-free person with $110,000

00:11:27.770 --> 00:11:31.429
can borrow $11,000

00:11:31.429 --> 00:11:34.070
and can spend $121,000,

00:11:34.070 --> 00:11:38.170
even though they only earned $110,000.

00:11:38.170 --> 00:11:40.640
Your spending is someone else's income,

00:11:40.640 --> 00:11:43.430
and by following the transactions,

00:11:43.430 --> 00:11:45.430
we begin to see how this process

00:11:45.430 --> 00:11:47.430
works in a self-confirming pattern.

00:11:47.830 --> 00:11:51.600
But don't forget that borrowing money creates cycles.

00:11:51.600 --> 00:11:55.809
And if the cycle goes up, it has to come down again at some point.

00:11:56.009 --> 00:11:59.710
This brings us to the short-term debt cycle.

00:12:00.810 --> 00:12:04.380
With increasing economic activity, we see an expansion

00:12:04.380 --> 00:12:06.840
-- the first phase of the short-term debt cycle.

00:12:06.840 --> 00:12:10.720
Spending continues to rise, and prices are following suit.

00:12:10.720 --> 00:12:15.230
This happens because the increased spending is fueled by loans,

00:12:15.230 --> 00:12:17.450
which can be created instantly out of thin air.

00:12:17.450 --> 00:12:22.680
When spending and income grow faster than goods production,

00:12:22.680 --> 00:12:23.880
prices rise.

00:12:23.880 --> 00:12:28.000
When prices rise, we call that inflation.

00:12:28.000 --> 00:12:32.500
The central bank does not want high inflation,

00:12:32.500 --> 00:12:35.010
as this creates problems.

00:12:35.010 --> 00:12:38.250
A price increase raises interest rates.

00:12:38.250 --> 00:12:42.959
Higher interest rates mean fewer people can borrow money,

00:12:42.959 --> 00:12:45.600
and the cost of existing debt increases.

00:12:45.600 --> 00:12:50.100
Imagine it as if your credit card monthly payment is increasing.

00:12:50.100 --> 00:12:54.459
Since less money is borrowed and debt repayments are higher,

00:12:54.459 --> 00:12:58.720
less money remains, and expenses decrease.

00:12:58.720 --> 00:13:02.779
And since one person's expenses are another person's income,

00:13:02.779 --> 00:13:06.589
incomes decrease...and so on and so forth.

00:13:06.589 --> 00:13:10.800
When you spend less, prices fall.

00:13:10.800 --> 00:13:12.689
We call that deflation.

00:13:12.689 --> 00:13:17.460
The economy is slowing down and we are in a recession.

00:13:17.460 --> 00:13:20.060
If the recession becomes too severe

00:13:20.060 --> 00:13:22.440
and inflation is no longer a problem,

00:13:22.440 --> 00:13:27.060
the central bank lowers interest rates to allow the economy to recover.

00:13:27.060 --> 00:13:29.650
With low interest rates

00:13:29.650 --> 00:13:30.650
, repayment amounts decrease,

00:13:30.650 --> 00:13:33.250
borrowing and consumption pick up again,

00:13:33.250 --> 00:13:35.450
and we experience another expansion.

00:13:35.450 --> 00:13:39.450
As you can see, the economy works like a machine.

00:13:40.250 --> 00:13:44.160
In the short-term debt cycle, consumption is only restrained by the willingness

00:13:44.160 --> 00:13:47.140
of lenders and borrowers to give and take loans.

00:13:47.140 --> 00:13:52.510
When loans are easy to obtain, the economy expands.

00:13:52.510 --> 00:13:56.090
If not, there will be a recession.

00:13:56.090 --> 00:14:00.450
Note that this cycle is primarily controlled by the central bank.

00:14:00.450 --> 00:14:05.120
The short-term debt cycle typically lasts 5-8 years

00:14:05.120 --> 00:14:08.410
and repeats itself repeatedly for decades.

00:14:08.410 --> 00:14:10.410
Note, however, that the end

00:14:10.410 --> 00:14:12.400
and beginning of each cycle

00:14:12.400 --> 00:14:16.670
produce more growth and debt than its predecessor.

00:14:16.670 --> 00:14:18.040
Why?

00:14:18.040 --> 00:14:20.740
Because people push it forward

00:14:20.740 --> 00:14:25.530
-- they have a tendency to borrow and spend more instead of paying their debts.

00:14:25.530 --> 00:14:27.480
It's human nature.

00:14:27.480 --> 00:14:29.380
Therefore, in the

00:14:29.380 --> 00:14:30.680
long term,

00:14:30.680 --> 00:14:33.470
debts rise faster than incomes.

00:14:33.470 --> 00:14:36.670
This creates the long-term debt cycle.

00:14:38.070 --> 00:14:39.670
Although people are becoming increasingly indebted,

00:14:40.170 --> 00:14:44.030
lenders are granting loans more and more freely.

00:14:44.030 --> 00:14:45.030
Why?

00:14:45.030 --> 00:14:48.670
Because everyone thinks everything is going great!

00:14:48.670 --> 00:14:51.970
People are only focusing on what has recently happened.

00:14:51.970 --> 00:14:55.650
And what happened recently?

00:14:55.650 --> 00:14:57.650
Incomes have increased!

00:14:57.650 --> 00:14:59.250
Asset values ​​are rising!

00:14:59.250 --> 00:15:01.550
The stock market is booming!

00:15:01.550 --> 00:15:02.480
We're having a boom!

00:15:02.480 --> 00:15:06.690
It's worthwhile to buy goods, services, and equipment –

00:15:06.690 --> 00:15:08.390
with borrowed money!

00:15:08.390 --> 00:15:11.770
When this gets out of hand, we call it a bubble.  So

00:15:11.770 --> 00:15:14.640
although debts have increased,

00:15:14.640 --> 00:15:18.110
incomes have risen almost as fast to offset them.

00:15:18.110 --> 00:15:21.970
Let's call the ratio of debt to income the debt burden.

00:15:21.970 --> 00:15:25.210
As long as income continues to rise,

00:15:25.210 --> 00:15:27.040
the debt burden remains manageable.

00:15:27.040 --> 00:15:30.230
At the same time, asset values ​​are skyrocketing.

00:15:30.230 --> 00:15:33.230
People are taking out huge loans to

00:15:34.030 --> 00:15:35.060
buy investment assets

00:15:35.060 --> 00:15:37.660
that make them even more expensive.

00:15:37.660 --> 00:15:40.260
People feel rich,

00:15:40.260 --> 00:15:43.260
so even with the accumulation of high debts,

00:15:43.260 --> 00:15:49.490
rising incomes and assets help debtors to remain creditworthy for a long time.

00:15:49.490 --> 00:15:52.530
But of course, this cannot continue indefinitely.

00:15:52.530 --> 00:15:54.250
It doesn't!

00:15:54.250 --> 00:16:00.520
Over the years, the debt burden slowly increases and the repayment amounts rise.

00:16:00.520 --> 00:16:05.400
Eventually, loan repayments grow faster than income,

00:16:05.400 --> 00:16:08.240
forcing people to pay.  to cut their spending.

00:16:08.240 --> 00:16:12.200
And since one person's expenses are another person's income,

00:16:12.200 --> 00:16:14.500
incomes decrease...

00:16:14.500 --> 00:16:19.020
...which leads to lower creditworthiness and fewer loans.

00:16:19.020 --> 00:16:22.020
Loan repayments continue to rise,

00:16:22.020 --> 00:16:24.440
spending is further reduced...

00:16:24.440 --> 00:16:27.140
...and the cycle reverses.

00:16:27.140 --> 00:16:30.960
This is the long-term peak in debt.

00:16:30.960 --> 00:16:34.150
The debt burden has simply become too great.

00:16:34.150 --> 00:16:38.830
For the USA, Europe, and most of the rest of the world, this happened in

00:16:38.830 --> 00:16:40.760
2008.

00:16:40.760 --> 00:16:45.430
It happened for the same reason as in Japan in 1989,

00:16:45.430 --> 00:16:48.750
and in the USA in 1929.

00:16:48.750 --> 00:16:51.980
Now the economy is beginning to reduce its debt.

00:16:51.980 --> 00:16:56.500
Debt reduction means: less spending,

00:16:56.500 --> 00:16:59.540
incomes fall, credit disappears,

00:16:59.540 --> 00:17:02.700
investment prices fall, banks come under pressure,

00:17:02.700 --> 00:17:06.340
the stock market collapses, social tensions arise,

00:17:06.340 --> 00:17:09.709
and the whole system begins to eat itself up in reverse.

00:17:09.709 --> 00:17:13.850
When incomes fall and loan repayments increase,

00:17:13.850 --> 00:17:17.990
borrowers come under pressure.  If they are no longer creditworthy,

00:17:17.990 --> 00:17:22.360
the loan disappears and the borrowers do not have enough money

00:17:22.360 --> 00:17:23.600
for their repayments.

00:17:23.600 --> 00:17:28.440
To fill the gap, they are forced to sell their assets.

00:17:28.440 --> 00:17:31.550
The market is flooded with a surge in asset sales, while spending is declining.

00:17:31.550 --> 00:17:36.370
At this point, the stock market collapses,

00:17:36.370 --> 00:17:39.740
the real estate market crashes, and the banks get into trouble.

00:17:39.740 --> 00:17:44.940
When asset values ​​decline, the value of the debtors' collateral also declines.

00:17:44.940 --> 00:17:48.280
That makes them even less creditworthy.

00:17:48.280 --> 00:17:50.200
People feel destitute.  A

00:17:51.300 --> 00:17:55.010
rapid decline in credit is occurring.  Less consumption &gt;

00:17:55.010 --> 00:17:55.890
less income &gt;

00:17:55.890 --> 00:17:57.890
less wealth &gt;

00:17:57.890 --> 00:17:58.590
less credit &gt;

00:17:58.590 --> 00:18:00.800
less borrowing, etc.

00:18:00.800 --> 00:18:03.000
It's a vicious cycle.

00:18:03.000 --> 00:18:06.530
It appears similar to a recession, but the difference

00:18:06.530 --> 00:18:10.160
is that interest rates cannot be lowered as a lifeline.

00:18:10.160 --> 00:18:14.590
In a recession, lowering interest rates stimulates borrowing.

00:18:14.590 --> 00:18:18.570
However, the interest rate cut is of no use in reducing debt, because

00:18:18.570 --> 00:18:20.530
interest rates are already

00:18:20.530 --> 00:18:25.310
low, almost at 0% - so the stimulation ends.

00:18:25.310 --> 00:18:29.210
Interest rates in the US fell to 0% during the debt reduction of

00:18:29.210 --> 00:18:30.840
the 1930s,

00:18:30.840 --> 00:18:33.440
and again in 2008.

00:18:33.440 --> 00:18:35.840
The difference between a recession

00:18:35.840 --> 00:18:40.270
and debt reduction is that in debt reduction, the debtor

00:18:40.270 --> 00:18:41.930
is simply too heavily indebted

00:18:41.930 --> 00:18:45.050
and cannot be relieved by an interest rate cut.

00:18:45.050 --> 00:18:50.240
Lenders realize that the debts have become too high to ever be fully repaid.

00:18:50.240 --> 00:18:55.310
The debtors are no longer able to repay and their collateral has lost value.

00:18:55.310 --> 00:18:59.370
They feel hindered by guilt and don't want to do anything anymore!

00:18:59.370 --> 00:19:03.490
Interest wanes among both lenders and borrowers.  Imagine

00:19:03.490 --> 00:19:07.020
the economy as being uncreditworthy,

00:19:07.020 --> 00:19:09.000
similar to a person.  So

00:19:09.000 --> 00:19:12.600
what do you do when reducing debt?

00:19:12.600 --> 00:19:17.540
The problem is that the debt burden is too high and needs to be reduced.

00:19:17.540 --> 00:19:20.790
This can happen in four different ways.

00:19:20.790 --> 00:19:24.489
1. People, businesses, and the state are scaling back.

00:19:24.489 --> 00:19:28.409
2. Debts are reduced through payment defaults and restructuring.

00:19:28.409 --> 00:19:34.139
3. Wealth is redistributed from the "rich" to the "poor".

00:19:34.139 --> 00:19:37.980
And finally, 4. The central bank prints new money.

00:19:37.980 --> 00:19:42.999
These four approaches have been used in every debt reduction process in modern history.

00:19:45.699 --> 00:19:47.779
As a rule, expenses are cut first.

00:19:47.879 --> 00:19:52.129
As mentioned, individuals, businesses, banks, and even the government are cutting back

00:19:52.129 --> 00:19:54.869
and reducing their spending in order to pay off their debts.

00:19:54.869 --> 00:19:58.559
This is often referred to as austerity policy.

00:19:58.559 --> 00:20:01.830
If borrowers stop taking out new loans

00:20:01.830 --> 00:20:06.769
and start paying off old debts, one would expect the debt burden to decrease.

00:20:06.769 --> 00:20:10.720
But the opposite happens!  Because spending is curbed

00:20:10.720 --> 00:20:14.610
- and one person's spending is another person's income -- which

00:20:14.610 --> 00:20:19.029
leads to lower incomes.  They fall faster than the repayment;

00:20:19.029 --> 00:20:23.210
The debt burden will actually increase.  We have seen that

00:20:23.210 --> 00:20:26.330
this spending cut is deflationary and painful.

00:20:26.330 --> 00:20:29.389
Companies are forced to cut costs...

00:20:29.389 --> 00:20:32.779
which means less work and higher unemployment.

00:20:32.779 --> 00:20:37.139
This leads to the next step: the debts must be reduced!

00:20:37.139 --> 00:20:41.149
Many borrowers are unable to repay their loans

00:20:41.149 --> 00:20:44.299
-- and the borrowers' debts are the lenders' assets.

00:20:44.299 --> 00:20:48.749
When borrowers fail to make repayments to the bank, there are fears that the bank

00:20:48.749 --> 00:20:50.309
could become insolvent.  There is

00:20:50.309 --> 00:20:54.909
a run on the banks.  Banks are under pressure, and

00:20:54.909 --> 00:20:55.590
people,

00:20:55.590 --> 00:21:00.080
businesses, and banks are falling into arrears.  This serious

00:21:00.080 --> 00:21:03.570
economic downturn is a depression.

00:21:03.570 --> 00:21:08.649
During a depression, people mainly discover that their

00:21:08.649 --> 00:21:11.089
supposed wealth does not exist.

00:21:11.089 --> 00:21:13.490
Let's go back to the bar.

00:21:13.690 --> 00:21:17.619
When you order a beer and have it put on your tab, you are

00:21:17.619 --> 00:21:23.570
promising the bartender you will pay.  Her promise will become the bartender's "fortune".

00:21:23.570 --> 00:21:28.129
If you don't keep your promise -- if you don't pay, and essentially

00:21:28.129 --> 00:21:29.309
skip out on your bill --

00:21:29.309 --> 00:21:32.649
then his alleged "wealth" is worthless.

00:21:32.649 --> 00:21:35.779
Basically, it no longer exists.

00:21:35.779 --> 00:21:39.710
Many lenders are reluctant to see their assets disappear and are willing to

00:21:39.710 --> 00:21:40.759
restructure their debt.

00:21:40.759 --> 00:21:44.320
Debt restructuring means lower repayments,

00:21:44.320 --> 00:21:48.049
over longer periods,

00:21:48.049 --> 00:21:52.330
or at lower interest rates than originally agreed.  Somehow,

00:21:52.330 --> 00:21:56.889
a breach of contract leads to debt reduction.  The creditor prefers a

00:21:56.889 --> 00:21:59.419
bird in the hand to two in the bush.

00:21:59.419 --> 00:22:03.450
Although the debt decreases, debt restructuring leads to a

00:22:03.450 --> 00:22:06.559
faster decline in income and assets,

00:22:06.559 --> 00:22:09.679
and the debt burden worsens further.

00:22:09.679 --> 00:22:12.950
Like spending cuts, debt reduction is also

00:22:12.950 --> 00:22:16.009
painful and deflationary.

00:22:16.009 --> 00:22:21.940
All of this affects the central government -- less income, less work

00:22:21.940 --> 00:22:27.049
means less tax revenue.

00:22:27.049 --> 00:22:30.210
At the same time, expenses are rising due to increasing unemployment.

00:22:30.210 --> 00:22:33.960
Many unemployed people have hardly any savings

00:22:33.960 --> 00:22:36.419
and need government support.

00:22:36.419 --> 00:22:39.999
In addition, there are government support packages

00:22:39.999 --> 00:22:43.879
that further increase spending to help the economy.

00:22:43.879 --> 00:22:47.509
The government budget deficit explodes during

00:22:47.509 --> 00:22:51.059
debt reduction because spending is higher than tax revenue.

00:22:51.059 --> 00:22:55.720
This is what happens when news reports about the budget deficit.

00:22:55.720 --> 00:23:01.320
To finance the deficit, either taxes

00:23:01.320 --> 00:23:06.059
or debt must be increased.  But where will the money come from when revenues are falling and

00:23:06.059 --> 00:23:09.789
unemployment is high?  From the rich.

00:23:09.789 --> 00:23:14.580
Since the state needs more money and wealth is concentrated in the hands of

00:23:14.580 --> 00:23:17.109
a small percentage of the population,

00:23:17.109 --> 00:23:20.379
the state increases taxes on the rich,

00:23:20.379 --> 00:23:24.450
which facilitates the redistribution of wealth in the economy --

00:23:24.450 --> 00:23:29.279
from the "rich" to the "poor".  The suffering "poor" begin

00:23:29.279 --> 00:23:30.970
to hate the rich.

00:23:30.970 --> 00:23:36.309
The rich, beset by the weak economy -- falling asset values,

00:23:36.309 --> 00:23:39.940
higher taxes - are beginning to hate the "poor".

00:23:39.940 --> 00:23:43.890
Persistent depression can lead to social unrest.

00:23:43.890 --> 00:23:47.280
Tensions are not only rising within the country,

00:23:47.280 --> 00:23:52.200
they can also spread across borders -- especially between creditor and debtor countries.

00:23:52.200 --> 00:23:56.040
This can lead to political changes,

00:23:56.040 --> 00:23:58.840
which can sometimes be extreme.

00:23:58.840 --> 00:24:02.630
In the 1930s, this led to Hitler's rise to power,

00:24:02.630 --> 00:24:08.080
war in Europe, and the economic crisis in the USA.   The pressure to end

00:24:08.080 --> 00:24:10.070
the economic crisis is increasing.

00:24:10.070 --> 00:24:14.950
Remember, what people perceived as wealth was actually credit.  So

00:24:14.950 --> 00:24:18.400
if the credit disappears, people don't have enough money.

00:24:18.400 --> 00:24:23.190
People desperately need money.  Do you remember who can print money?

00:24:23.190 --> 00:24:27.370
The central bank.

00:24:27.370 --> 00:24:30.309
After lowering interest rates to almost 0%,

00:24:30.309 --> 00:24:34.090
it is forced to print money.  Unlike spending cuts,

00:24:34.090 --> 00:24:37.299
debt reduction, and wealth redistribution,

00:24:37.299 --> 00:24:42.190
printing money is inflationary and promotes economic growth.  Inevitably, the

00:24:42.190 --> 00:24:43.210
central bank prints new money - out of thin

00:24:43.210 --> 00:24:47.150
air -- and uses it to buy financial assets

00:24:47.150 --> 00:24:52.260
and government bonds.  This happened during the economic crisis in the USA,

00:24:52.260 --> 00:24:56.010
and again in 2008, when the US central bank --

00:24:56.010 --> 00:24:59.940
the Federal Reserve -- printed over 2 trillion dollars.

00:24:59.940 --> 00:25:04.179
Other central banks around the world that could, also printed a lot of money.

00:25:04.179 --> 00:25:07.440
Buying financial assets with the money

00:25:07.440 --> 00:25:11.679
allows prices to rise, which makes people creditworthy again.

00:25:11.679 --> 00:25:15.820
However, it only helps those who own financial assets.

00:25:15.820 --> 00:25:21.840
Because the central bank can print money, but can only buy financial assets.

00:25:21.840 --> 00:25:24.900
The central government, on the other hand,

00:25:24.900 --> 00:25:29.580
can buy goods and services and distribute the money to the population.

00:25:29.580 --> 00:25:34.520
But she can't print money.  Therefore, in order to stimulate the economy,

00:25:34.520 --> 00:25:35.650
both sides must cooperate.

00:25:35.650 --> 00:25:40.470
By buying government bonds, the central bank lends

00:25:40.470 --> 00:25:41.190
money to the state,

00:25:41.190 --> 00:25:44.909
allowing it to run a deficit and increase spending

00:25:44.909 --> 00:25:48.650
on goods and services through stimulus programs

00:25:48.650 --> 00:25:53.080
and unemployment benefits.  National income is rising,

00:25:53.080 --> 00:25:56.240
but so are national debts.  However,

00:25:56.240 --> 00:25:59.540
it helps to reduce the overall debt burden of the economy.

00:25:59.540 --> 00:26:05.429
This is a very risky time.  Decision-makers must weigh the four ways to

00:26:05.429 --> 00:26:06.590
reduce the debt burden.

00:26:06.590 --> 00:26:13.050
Deflationary measures must balance inflationary measures

00:26:13.050 --> 00:26:14.710
in order to maintain stability.

00:26:14.710 --> 00:26:18.130
With proper balancing, this can

00:26:18.130 --> 00:26:21.479
lead to a significant reduction in debt.

00:26:21.479 --> 00:26:25.359
You see, debt reduction can be horrible or beautiful.

00:26:25.359 --> 00:26:28.839
How can debt reduction be beautiful?

00:26:28.839 --> 00:26:33.429
Although debt reduction is a difficult situation,

00:26:33.429 --> 00:26:37.549
handling it in the best possible way can be beautiful.

00:26:37.549 --> 00:26:42.210
Better than the debt-ridden, unbalanced excesses of the

00:26:42.210 --> 00:26:45.940
debt phase.  With good debt reduction,

00:26:45.940 --> 00:26:51.089
debt decreases relative to income, real economic growth is positive,

00:26:51.089 --> 00:26:56.889
and inflation is not a problem.  This is achieved through proper balancing.

00:26:56.889 --> 00:27:00.159
The right balance requires a certain mix

00:27:00.159 --> 00:27:04.229
of spending cuts, debt reduction and wealth transfer,

00:27:04.229 --> 00:27:09.149
as well as the pressure of money to maintain economic and social stability.

00:27:09.149 --> 00:27:13.639
One wonders whether printing money increases inflation.

00:27:13.639 --> 00:27:18.879
No, not if it compensates for the lack of credit.  You know how it is – it's the expenses that matter.

00:27:18.879 --> 00:27:24.249
A dollar spent in cash has the same effect on the price as a dollar

00:27:24.249 --> 00:27:25.969
spent via credit payment.

00:27:25.969 --> 00:27:31.299
By printing money, the central bank can compensate for the lack of credit

00:27:31.299 --> 00:27:33.080
with more money.

00:27:33.080 --> 00:27:38.509
To achieve a recovery, the central bank must not only

00:27:38.509 --> 00:27:39.519
promote income growth,

00:27:39.519 --> 00:27:43.849
but also increase the growth rate of revenues via the interest rate of

00:27:43.849 --> 00:27:45.099
debt accumulation.

00:27:45.099 --> 00:27:48.379
What do I mean by that?  In principle,

00:27:48.379 --> 00:27:52.309
income must grow faster than debt.  For example, let's assume

00:27:52.309 --> 00:27:56.080
a country that is reducing its debt has a debt-to-

00:27:56.080 --> 00:27:58.580
income ratio of 100%.

00:27:58.580 --> 00:28:03.659
This means that the amount of his debt is equivalent to the annual income of the

00:28:03.659 --> 00:28:05.799
entire country.

00:28:05.799 --> 00:28:09.009
Now imagine the interest rate on this debt.  Let's say it's

00:28:09.009 --> 00:28:11.159
at 2%.

00:28:11.159 --> 00:28:15.029
If the debt grows by 2% due to interest and

00:28:15.029 --> 00:28:15.690
the income

00:28:15.690 --> 00:28:20.230
only by about 1%, you will never reduce the debt burden.

00:28:20.230 --> 00:28:24.809
They need to print enough money to raise the income rate above the

00:28:24.809 --> 00:28:25.950
interest rate.

00:28:25.950 --> 00:28:30.720
However, printing money can easily be abused because it is easy and

00:28:30.720 --> 00:28:33.049
people prefer it to alternatives.

00:28:33.049 --> 00:28:36.200
The point is not to print too much money

00:28:36.200 --> 00:28:41.110
and to avoid causing undesirably high inflation, as happened in Germany during

00:28:41.110 --> 00:28:43.129
the debt reduction of the 1920s.

00:28:43.129 --> 00:28:48.269
If decision-makers strike the right balance, debt reduction is not so dramatic.

00:28:48.269 --> 00:28:51.340
Growth is slow, but the debt burden is decreasing.

00:28:51.340 --> 00:28:54.470
That's a nice way to reduce debt.

00:28:54.470 --> 00:28:59.830
When incomes rise, borrowers appear more creditworthy again.

00:28:59.830 --> 00:29:02.999
And when these individuals appear more creditworthy again,

00:29:02.999 --> 00:29:08.509
lenders will begin offering loans again.  The debt burden is beginning to decrease.

00:29:08.509 --> 00:29:13.499
People can borrow money and spend more again, the economy starts

00:29:13.499 --> 00:29:14.399
to grow again,

00:29:14.399 --> 00:29:18.009
leading to the reflation phase of the long-term debt cycle.

00:29:18.009 --> 00:29:22.490
Although a poorly executed debt reduction process can be terrible,

00:29:22.490 --> 00:29:26.279
if handled correctly, the problem can eventually be resolved.

00:29:26.279 --> 00:29:29.580
It takes approximately a decade or more to

00:29:29.580 --> 00:29:33.669
reduce the debt burden and normalize the economy

00:29:33.669 --> 00:29:37.899
- hence the term "lost decade".

00:29:37.899 --> 00:29:42.720
In conclusion: Of course, the economy is a little more complicated than this guide

00:29:42.720 --> 00:29:43.639
suggests.

00:29:43.639 --> 00:29:48.850
However, if you overlay the short-term debt cycle onto the long-term cycle

00:29:48.850 --> 00:29:52.629
and then overlay both onto the productivity growth line,

00:29:52.629 --> 00:29:55.919
this provides a relatively good guide to see where we were,

00:29:55.919 --> 00:29:58.919
where we are now, and where we are likely to be headed.  In short, there are

00:29:58.919 --> 00:30:03.019
three rules of thumb I

00:30:03.019 --> 00:30:03.720
would like to share with you:

00:30:03.720 --> 00:30:08.220
First: Don't let your debts increase faster than your income,

00:30:08.220 --> 00:30:11.429
otherwise your debts will one day crush you.

00:30:11.429 --> 00:30:16.059
Secondly: Don't let income rise faster than productivity,

00:30:16.059 --> 00:30:19.159
otherwise you will one day be uncompetitive.

00:30:19.159 --> 00:30:24.000
And thirdly: Do everything you can to increase your productivity,

00:30:24.000 --> 00:30:29.029
because in the long run that's what matters.

00:30:29.549 --> 00:30:34.080
These are simple tips for you and also for political decision-makers.

00:30:34.080 --> 00:30:38.470
You may be surprised, but most people -- including political decision-makers -- do

00:30:38.470 --> 00:30:39.509
not pay enough attention to this.

00:30:39.509 --> 00:30:44.059
This guide has served me well and I hope it helps you too.

00:30:44.059 --> 00:30:46.380
Thanks.

